flowchart TD
  subgraph L0["Level 0 · Question"]
    Q["<b>Do tariffs change the trade balance,<br/>and who absorbed the Q4 US demand drop?</b><br/><i>Brad Setser, CFR, Feb 2020</i>"]
  end

  subgraph L1["Level 1 · Priors & assumptions"]
    P2["<b>Tariff revenue is not offset</b><br/>Trade scholars assume it is; Setser says not necessarily"]
    P3["<b>Few substitutes for China goods</b><br/>So the tariffs work as a clear tax"]
    P1["<b>Trade balance = saving − investment</b><br/><i>Never stated, but the argument depends on it</i>"]
    P4["<b>Tariff uncertainty weighs on firms</b><br/>Uncertainty can reduce investment"]
  end

  subgraph L2["Level 2 · Evidence"]
    D1["<b>Tariff revenue ~$30B → ~$80B a year</b><br/>~15% average tariff on $500B+ of China imports"]
    D2["<b>Fajgelbaum et al.</b><br/>Govt captures 35bp of the 60bp GDP consumers lose"]
    D3["<b>Bussière et al. + chart</b><br/>Investment slowdowns lead to import slowdowns"]
    D4["<b>Q4 imports weak</b><br/>Consumer goods, autos, capital goods all soft"]
    D5["<b>Vietnam exports to US +$17.5B</b><br/>Far short of the fall in China imports"]
  end

  subgraph L3["Level 3 · Mechanisms"]
    M1["<b>Tariffs act as a consumption tax</b><br/>Backdoor fiscal tightening slows consumption"]
    M2["<b>Uncertainty cuts capex</b><br/>Especially new business equipment"]
    M3["<b>Lower capex → lower imports</b><br/>Weaker investment means fewer imported goods"]
  end

  subgraph L4["Level 4 · Intermediate claims"]
    C1["<b>Tariffs cut the deficit by slowing growth</b><br/>Not the argument Trump makes for them"]
    C2["<b>Diversion no longer offsets China</b><br/>Imports from other countries stopped making up the gap"]
  end

  subgraph L5["Level 5 · Conclusion"]
    K["<b>Main claim: the US demand shock was exported</b><br/>Setser: #quot;the weakening of U.S. demand was felt globally,<br/>rather than in the United States#quot;<br/>US GDP held because services demand stayed strong"]
  end

  subgraph L6["Level 6 · Dialectic"]
    X["<b>Consensus: tariffs move level, not balance</b><br/>Setser admits he glossed over this too"]
    QF["<b>COVID confound</b><br/>Blip or persistent trend? Too early to tell"]
    R1["<b>Rival causes of weak capex</b><br/>Strong dollar, 2018 Fed hikes, shale cutbacks"]
  end

  P2 --> M1
  P3 --> M1
  D1 --> M1
  D2 --> M1
  P4 --> M2
  M2 --> M3
  D3 --> M3
  M1 --> C1
  M3 --> C1
  P1 -->|licenses| C1
  D4 --> C2
  D5 --> C2
  C1 --> K
  C2 --> K

  K -.->|qualifies| X
  K -. limited by .- QF
  M2 -. undercut by .- R1

  Q ~~~ P2 & P3 & P1 & P4
  P2 ~~~ D1
  P3 ~~~ D2
  P4 ~~~ D3
  P1 ~~~ D4 & D5
  D4 ~~~ M3
  D5 ~~~ M3

